// A peer whose field of 1024 under a window scale of 7 states 131072 bytes: a write of 80000, more than an unscaled
// window could hold, leaves whole, 55 segments of 1448 and one of 360, with no congestion control and a send cap of
// 64 entries to hold them. Linux would send the same bytes, starting at its initial congestion window.
